@startuml lockfree-path-copy-cat
' ============================================================================
' lockfree-path-copy-cat.puml — inserting "cat" copies ONLY the root→leaf spine
' it touches (A→C′→D′); the untouched 'a'→B subtree is shared by Arc pointer
' between the old root A and the new root A′. One atomic CAS publishes A → A′.
' Source: §Phase 1 (Build New Tree Structure) of lockfree-cas-artrie.md.
' Color key (house palette + persistence accents):
'   grey   #ECEFF1  old (superseded) version
'   teal   #B2DFDB  the path-copied new spine (A′, C′, D′)
'   green  #C8E6C9  the SHARED subtree B (pointed to by BOTH roots — no copy)
'   red    #FFCDD2  the single publishing CAS
' ============================================================================
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontColor #212121
  BorderThickness 1.3
}

title Insert **"cat"** — copy the touched spine, share the rest, publish by one CAS

package "BEFORE — old root A" #F5F5F5 {
  rectangle "**A**  (old root)\n'a' → B    ·    'c' → ∅  (no child)" as A #ECEFF1
  rectangle "**B**  subtree" as B #C8E6C9
  A -down-> B : a
}

package "AFTER — new root A′  (path-copied)" #F1F8F4 {
  rectangle "**A′**  (new root)\n'a' → B (shared)   ·   'c' → C′" as Ap #B2DFDB
  rectangle "**C′**  (new)\n'a' → D′" as Cp #B2DFDB
  rectangle "**D′**  (new leaf, FINAL = 'cat')" as Dp #B2DFDB
  Ap -down-> Cp : c
  Cp -down-> Dp : a … t
}

Ap -[#2E7D32,bold]-> B : 'a' — **shared Arc**\n(no copy)
A =[#C62828]=> Ap : **CAS**(root: A → A′)\n= the linearization point

note bottom of Dp
  Only the O(|key|) spine A′·C′·D′ is allocated.
  Subtree B and everything else is shared by
  pointer, so both roots coexist until the old
  one is unreferenced (Arc refcount → 0).
end note
@enduml
